%% D4. Specifying time, random effects and residual correlation
%% A guide to reasoning, not an automatic rule for choosing a model.
flowchart TD
  A["Few fixed occasions shared by all, and the shape of change unknown?"] -->|Yes| T1["Time as a factor in the mean model; estimand = contrast at chosen visits"]
  A -->|"No: many or irregular times"| T2["Continuous time: linear, polynomial, piecewise or spline (Module 9), using actual times"]
  T1 --> C["Centre time where the intercept and group effects are meaningful"]
  T2 --> C
  C --> R["Random effects: do individuals plausibly differ in level? in rate of change?"]
  R --> R1["Random intercept"]
  R --> R2["Random intercept and slope on actual time"]
  R1 --> S["Correlation left after the random effects? Closely spaced visits suggest serial correlation"]
  R2 --> S
  S --> S1["Independent residuals"]
  S --> S2["AR(1) or exponential in actual time; heterogeneous variances"]
  S --> S3["Unstructured covariance without random effects (few occasions, many subjects)"]
  S1 --> V["Compare the implied marginal covariance V = Z G Z^T + R with the observed covariance; REML comparisons need the same fixed effects (Module 5)"]
  S2 --> V
  S3 --> V
  V --> W["Prefer the simplest adequate model and check that conclusions are stable"]
  classDef q fill:#ffffff,stroke:#555555,color:#222222;
  classDef m fill:#eef4f8,stroke:#0b5d8f,color:#222222;
  class A,C,R,S,V q;
  class T1,T2,R1,R2,S1,S2,S3,W m;
